        "committer": {
          "name": "Patrickbot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-10-29 22:08:49.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: speed up sanityn test_41i",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: speed up sanityn test_41i\n\nsanityn test_41i runs 100 create vs create iterations for each of\ntwo fail_locs and takes about 730 seconds in CI.  The 0x169 half\ntakes about 130 seconds, as the race fires.  The 0x16a half takes\nabout 600 seconds: mdt_open_lock_mode() looks the name up before\nlocking, so both creates ask for a PW lock on the parent, the\nsecond blocks, and the OPEN2 race never forms.  Every iteration\nwaits the full 5 second cfs_race_loc() timeout.  Change 47506\n(LU-15907) is the real fix for that race, and 61704 (LU-17581)\nalso touches this test.\n\nRun 25 iterations for 0x169 and 10 for 0x16a.  Both fail_locs\nand the pass/fail checks are kept.\n\nOn a test VM, ONLY=41i took 556s and 573s before and 64s, 65s and\n64s after.  At about 500 seconds saved per run and 3881 runs per\n30 days that is about 540 hours of CI time per 30 days.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanityn env=ONLY=41i\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Ia279b4d34af9dabf395f99024f624abea2fe4887\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
